Call Back Verification means the BBS will call your computer back to
verify your phone number. First, you will be asked to enter the number
that will be called, (in case it's different from your "normal" number),
and then the BBS will hangup and call you back. When your phone rings,
(or your modem's RING light flashes, or you see RING on your terminal
screen) type  ATA  and press RETURN. You will then be asked for your
name and password again and, if you pass those requirements, you will
be validated as a member of this BBS with immediate access to the file
libraries, message conferences, and many more commands.

*** IF YOU FIRST DIALED A "1" TO CALL THIS BBS, CALLBACK WON'T WORK! ***
 
